# tqdm on long loops

When writing or launching multi-episode / multi-seed experiment or evaluation
scripts under `AICTFProject/experiments/`, wrap the main work loop with
`experiments.tqdm_loop.tqdm_iter` (stderr ETA). Do not use silent nested seed
loops.

- PPO training: already has SB3-style tqdm via `enable_progress_bar=True`
  (`rl.custom_ppo.trainer`); do not disable it for production runs.
- Prefer one flat progress bar over nested silent loops.
- Do not restart a one-shot sealed run just to add tqdm unless the user
  explicitly requests a restart before RESULT artifacts exist.
- Durable heartbeat (optional): `experiments/long_session_progress.py`.

